# Tracked/ignored split for the test-auth kit under PRPs/auth/.
#
# Why this exists: a Playwright storage-state file, a session file or a
# credential store can impersonate a test account. None of them may ever reach
# git history or a PR-bound report.
#
# Why .gitignore alone is not enough: it does not cover an already-tracked file,
# and a committed secret persists in history. auth-kit-secrecy.mjs therefore
# proves every secret path ignored with `git check-ignore` before any secret is
# written, and halts with FAILED_IGNORE_UNPROVEN otherwise.
#
# This file is copied to PRPs/auth/.gitignore, so every rule below is relative
# to PRPs/auth/. The tracked side (auth-model.md, the generated scripts,
# credentials.example.* and .gitignore itself) is deliberately not listed, so
# nothing else in PRPs/auth/ is ignored.
#
# Why the re-include works: `credentials.*` is a filename pattern, not a parent
# DIRECTORY exclusion, so git still reads the directory and the `!` rule takes
# effect (git never descends into an excluded directory).

# The credential store, in any format.
credentials.*
# The tracked placeholder that documents the credential store's shape.
!credentials.example.*

# Per-role session, storage-state and token artifacts.
.sessions/

# A storage-state or session file written outside .sessions/.
*.storage-state.json
*.session.json
